From 4366f05d5f6dc1b2ac32855d0347a79558c72499 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: parwa-dev <dev@parwa.local>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 12:36:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(auth): resilient Google sign-in + gated local session
 fallback
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- /api/auth/google: when the backend is unreachable or not configured,
  verify the id_token server-side via Google tokeninfo (same checks as
  backend _verify_google_token: aud, email_verified, exp) and issue a
  local session. Gated behind ENABLE_LOCAL_GOOGLE_AUTH=1 — prod behavior
  unchanged (backend stays sole issuer).
- /api/auth/me-proxy: local session verification fallback so logins
  survive backend outages.
- /api/auth/refresh: local refresh of locally-issued sessions.
- login page: NEXT_PUBLIC_SKIP_SUBSCRIPTION_CHECK=1 sends users straight
  to the dashboard after login (testing bypass for the Netflix-rule
  subscription gate).
- scripts/test-local-auth.ts: self-test for the fallback machinery
  (6/6 passing: forge rejection, upsert, mint, verify, refresh, persist).
